messages:
ashley: FYI I opened a docs PR (github.com/redwood/docs/pull/842) to add a minimal tracing-hook example for the Console -> Traces section. Needs review before we merge, esp the SDK snippet.

mike: looking now. what's the main problem?

ashley: snippet compiles but the tracing span names in the dashboard don't match the Console examples. I think the SDK call we show sets span.name = 'handler' but the runtime uses route names.

sara: can you paste the snippet?

ashley: sure:
```js
// docs/example/tracing-hook.js
const {Tracer} = require('@redwood/inference-sdk');
const tracer = new Tracer({service: 'console-demo'});

app.post('/invoke', async (req, res) => {
  const span = tracer.startSpan('handler');
  // call runtime
  await runtime.request(req.body);
  span.end();
  res.sendStatus(200);
});
```

mike: ah yep. the Console tracing docs expect spans tagged with `route:/invoke` and `model:...` so the example should startSpan(`route:${req.path}`) and add the model tag.

ryan: also noticed the PR has a link to /console/dashboards/cost-breakdown but that path changed in the latest site build. It 404s on the preview site.

ashley: ugh. I searched the site tree and found the new slug is /console/observability/cost-breakdown. I'll update the link in the PR.

mike: small nit — in the Cost/Latency breakdown example you use "p99 latency" but downstream code uses numeric percentiles like 0.99. Maybe show both ways?

ashley: good call. I'll add a note + example query for both: human-readable and PromQL style.

sara: For the tracing hook migration guide, can we add a short 2-line migration note: "If you previously called tracer.startSpan('handler'), change to tracer.startSpan(`route:${req.path}`) and set `span.setTag('model', modelId)` to match Console grouping." Keeps customers from having to re-map dashboards.

ashley: will add that. Also adding a tiny test snippet showing how prefix caching influences trace size (requested by support).

ryan: once you fix snippet and links pls ping me, I'll run the preview and check dashboards and the cost widget sample.

docs-bot: Preview site build for pull/842 queued. Status: pending (check https://ci.redwood.dev/builds/59812).

ashley: thanks — targeting a patch in 30m. If anyone has a one-liner we should include in the note for enterprise users (private deployments), drop it here.

mike: maybe: "For Private deployments, ensure your tracing collector endpoint is reachable from the VPC — Console assumes traces are forwarded to the configured OTLP endpoint." Short and useful.

ashley: perfect, adding that. will tag @ryan when pushed. :thumbsup:

sara: LGTM once links + span name fix are in.

